c Spec 104 fixture — REDUCED from release/basic/basic_kbdus (v1.2, the
c Keyman Developer template family). The source .kmn carries 97 key
c rules — every one for K_ keys (two kept verbatim below); NO rule in
c the source references any T_ id, while the source touch layout's
c symbol layer is built from T_<HEX> keys with keycap text and
c nextlayer only. Those rule-free T_<HEX> keys are the dead-key
c population of research.md §1/§2 (2,115 pairs corpus-wide): a T_ key
c has no fallback, so without a rule it types nothing.

store(&VERSION) '10.0'
store(&NAME) 'US Basic'
store(&COPYRIGHT) '© 2008-2020 SIL International'
store(&KEYBOARDVERSION) '1.2'
store(&LAYOUTFILE) 'basic_kbdus.keyman-touch-layout'
store(&TARGETS) 'any'

begin Unicode > use(main)

group(main) using keys

+ [K_SPACE] > U+0020
+ [K_0] > U+0030
+ [SHIFT K_0] > U+0029
